<title>HUNGARY: Danubius soars to record high.</title>
<headline>Danubius soars to record high.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The shares in Hungarian hotel chain Danubius Rt soared to a new all-time high on the Budapest bourse on Thursday after the Competition Office (CO) approved the purchase of a hotel chain by Danubius.</p>
<p>Danubius shares opened at 3,590 forints, and soared to a new all-time high of 3,945 forints. At 1059 GMT they stood at 3,780 forints.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a link between the surge of Danubius shares and the good news,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Trading in Danubius shares was suspended on Wednesday because the company could not confirm or deny press reports -- which were later confirmed by Reuters -- that the CO had approved Danubius' purchase of Hungaria Szalloda Rt.</p>
<p>-- Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom + 36 1 327-4040</p>
